</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8866fc30-aeb0-11f1-8ae9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CE72P.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8866fc30-aeb0-11f1-8ae9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CE72P.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ee9f6e44-ae68-11f1-af14-2bef011f780f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 05:15:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8866fc30-aeb0-11f1-8ae9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C7CE72P.jpg">© Tobias Schwarz, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky urges Trump to impose new Russia sanctions 'now', after deadly Ukraine strikes</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-zelensky-urges-trump-to-impose-new-russia-sanctions-now-after-deadly-ukraine-strikes</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Friday urged US President Donald Trump to impose new sanctions on Russia over deadly strikes on Ukraine, as Kyiv and Moscow step up attacks and US-led efforts to end the war remain deadlocked. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aaae0618-ae0f-11f1-9530-115fa1eedc7a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:13:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c23efbe-ae0f-11f1-929d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T104246Z-849861914-RC2MFNAOGGWF-RTRMADP-3-NORWAY-ROYALS-KING-HARALD-FUNERAL.jpg">© Leonhard Foeger, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Elections in Russia: the 1001 tricks to remove inconvenient candidates</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-elections-in-russia-the-1001-tricks-to-remove-inconvenient-candidates</link><description>
The Russian authorities are using dubious claims to disqualify candidates previously cleared to run in the parliamentary election from September 18 to 20. The war in Ukraine is making the Kremlin even more cautious about who is allowed to campaign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15b4f1e4-ac65-11f1-9416-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ruusia-elex-m.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15b4f1e4-ac65-11f1-9416-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ruusia-elex-m.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eed46b30-adf5-11f1-ad25-fdbeb0831cec</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:11:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/15b4f1e4-ac65-11f1-9416-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/ruusia-elex-m.jpg">© Ramil Sitdikov, Reuters </source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>I'm extremely worried by extremists that win elections in Europe: Luxembourg's PM Luc Frieden</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260911-i-m-extremely-worried-by-extremists-that-win-elections-in-europe-luxembourg-s-pm-luc-frieden</link><description>
"European strategic autonomy" is a buzz phrase in Brussels and in EU capitals these days. What does it mean for space policy? That was one of the central points that we raised with the Prime Minister of Luxembourg, Luc Frieden, during his visit to Paris for the International Space Summit hosted by the French government on September 9 and 10. Major American aerospace companies were noticeably absent from the summit while the feud between Brussels and the Trump administration continues.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2977ce88-ac63-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Frieden.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2977ce88-ac63-11f1-800d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Frieden.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0463475a-ab8f-11f1-8b94-d5f57f4dde63</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:53:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A fire destroys part of a migrant camp in the Spanish enclave of Ceuta</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-a-fire-destroys-part-of-a-migrant-camp-in-the-spanish-enclave-of-ceuta</link><description>
An apparently accidental fire destroyed about 40 shacks at a migrant camp in Ceuta, local media reported, but caused no injuries, Spanish police told AFP on Friday. The North African enclave saw tens of thousands of migrants arrive from Morocco in late July. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c01de1d6-adeb-11f1-80bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ceuta-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c01de1d6-adeb-11f1-80bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ceuta-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f59d6692-adeb-11f1-92db-1b3c08d9b68c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:41:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>French far-right leader polling ahead for 2027 election: should the EU be afraid?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/french-far-right-leader-polling-ahead-for-2027-election-should-the-eu-be-afraid</link><description>
In Brussels, opinion polls coming out of France have not escaped attention. Two polls see far right leader Marine Le Pen beating all her likely rivals in the French presidential election, which is set to take place in April and May of next year. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88174ede-ab8a-11f1-b537-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/260902-FR24-Talking-EU-2-div.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88174ede-ab8a-11f1-b537-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/260902-FR24-Talking-EU-2-div.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3cbf25f0-ab8b-11f1-8f22-d5f57f4dde63</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:14:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Did the War on Terror succeed? Or did Washington fall into al Qaeda’s trap?</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW: Friday, September 11– 25 years on from 9/11, the international press reflects on the war on terror, its legacy and its failings. In France, the far-right National Rally party tries desperately to distance itself from the overtly racist comments of one of its security officials, made while on duty for his day job as a police officer. Finally, a fossilised feather may give us new insights into why birds survived the asteroid that killed the dinosaurs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc3bd85c-adb2-11f1-9e7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11266649136aa3ae691c5b85-69544097.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc3bd85c-adb2-11f1-9e7e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-11266649136aa3ae691c5b85-69544097.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8271fe86-adb3-11f1-ace7-ff2b73643b37</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:16:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Italy's Emma Bonino, champion of battles to legalise abortion and divorce, dies at 78</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260911-italy-s-emma-bonino-champion-of-battles-to-legalise-abortion-and-divorce-dies-at-78</link><description>
Veteran feminist activist Emma Bonino, who rose to political prominence in the 1970s as a leader of campaigns to legalise abortion and divorce in heavily Roman Catholic Italy over the objections of the Vatican, has died aged 78. Bonino, who was diagnosed with lung cancer in 2015, served as foreign minister and European commissioner but failed in her bid to become Italy's first woman president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c26599e-adbb-11f1-8c36-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d6561e9b280d2b71a20f85bed864889f9ca57472.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c26599e-adbb-11f1-8c36-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d6561e9b280d2b71a20f85bed864889f9ca57472.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6d8266ca-adbb-11f1-a109-c5ee525281ed</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 08:33:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c26599e-adbb-11f1-8c36-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/d6561e9b280d2b71a20f85bed864889f9ca57472.jpg">© Tiziana Fabi, AFP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications</link><description>
From communications to crewed spaceflight, French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place in the space race on Thursday – notably, against the United States and China. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61141a3e-ad5a-11f1-a6a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-223109-224243-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61141a3e-ad5a-11f1-a6a0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-223109-224243-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">669954f6-ad5a-11f1-bdc4-23806945c836</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:03:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush</link><description>
Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746244e0-ad4a-11f1-9008-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T185030Z-175681737-RC2XANA20Z8P-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746244e0-ad4a-11f1-9008-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T185030Z-175681737-RC2XANA20Z8P-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">85cb6ac8-ad49-11f1-ad84-c5efca00c8f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:32:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/746244e0-ad4a-11f1-9008-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T185030Z-175681737-RC2XANA20Z8P-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Pedro Nunes, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
